menu "Monocle Configuration"

    config MONOCLE_FALLBACK_WIFI_SSID
        string "Development fallback Wi-Fi SSID"
        default "myssid"
        help
            Used only at boot, and only when NVS holds no credentials — the
            normal path is the app writing them to the wifi_creds
            characteristic over BLE. A successful join saves them to NVS,
            after which the stored copy wins and this is ignored.

            Leave it at the "myssid" placeholder to disable the fallback and
            always wait for the app.

    config MONOCLE_FALLBACK_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Development fallback Wi-Fi password"
        default "mypassword"
        help
            Passphrase for the fallback SSID above.

            Note this is stored in plaintext in sdkconfig. That file is
            gitignored, as is sdkconfig.old — a passphrase reached this
            repository's history through the latter once already.

    config MONOCLE_WIFI_MAX_RETRY
        int "Wi-Fi join attempts before giving up"
        default 5
        help
            How many times to retry a join before reporting failure over the
            wifi_state characteristic, so an absent or misconfigured network
            fails visibly instead of retrying forever.

    config MONOCLE_MIC_DUMP_AT_BOOT
        bool "Dump a few seconds of microphone audio at boot"
        default n
        help
            Development aid for milestone 3. Records from the mic shortly
            after boot and prints the PCM to the console as base64, which
            firmware/test/capture_mic.py turns into a WAV.

            The point is to prove the capture path produces intelligible
            audio before a wake word detector is wired to it — otherwise a
            silent pipeline has two possible causes and debugging it means
            guessing which.

            Off by default: it delays boot and prints ~130 KB to the console
            every time.

endmenu
